       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the recommended maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 800 mg per dose and 3,200 mg/day for adults, under prescription labeling.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose. It substantially raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **1600 mg/day total,** for example 400 mg four times daily.\n2. **The maximum anti-inflammatory dose,** 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day).\n3. **A different drug or dose,** if 1600 mg was meant for something else.\n4. **The dose as written.** If this is deliberate, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'll enter it with that note.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
